    - target: {fileID: 827748465615634449, guid: cb5c9ac9e8c24984f8e52c8939d90f9a, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "Like a lot of the animals hunted in the late neolithic, Aurochs weren\u2019t
        generally hunted for food. The main reasons we believe they were hunted was;
        to stop them ruining crops, and to prevent them breeding with the domesticated
        livestock. The size of the offspring would have likely cause problems with
        the birth."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
